                <div class="text-body-secondary" style="margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                    Washington State levies a tiered REET on property sales. Portions of the sale price are taxed progressively: 1.1% on amounts up to $525,000; 1.28% on portion between $525,000 and $1,525,000; 2.75% on portion between $1,525,000 and $3,025,000; and 3.0% on portion over $3,025,000 (plus local municipal surtaxes). You can model your exact WA REET breakdown using my <a href="/sellerproceeds/" style="color: var(--alpine-blue); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: underline;">Seller Net Proceeds Calculator</a>.
